&P350084 = ARM 10, 120 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. a-na {munus}szi-ib-tu 
#tr.ts: ana šibtu 
#tr.en: To Sibtu 
2. qi2-bi2-ma 
#tr.ts: qibima 
#tr.en: speak! 
3. um-ma be-el-ki-ma 
#tr.ts: umma bēlkima 
#tr.en: Thus your lord: 
4. asz-szum sza ki-a-am ta-asz-pu-ri-im 
#tr.ts: aššum ša kiam tašpurīm 
#tr.en: As to what you in the following way wrote me, 
5. um-ma at-ti-ma 
#tr.ts: umma attima 
#tr.en: thus you: 
6. i-na ba-ru-u2-tim 
#tr.ts: ina bārûtim 
#tr.en: In the divination 
7. sza _{gesz}tukul-mesz_ 
#tr.ts: ša kakkī 
#tr.en: of weapons 
8. a-na-ku et-me2-ku sza ta-asz-pu-ri-im 
#tr.ts: anāku etmêku ša tašpurīm 
#tr.en: I am occupied.” In that which you wrote me, 
9. i-na ba-ru-u2-tim-ma sza _{gesz}tukul-mesz_  
#tr.ts: ina bārûtimma ša kakkī 
#tr.en: in the very divination of weapons, 
10. et-me2-e-ti 
#tr.ts: etmêti 
#tr.en: you are occupied? 
11. am-mi-nim i-na ba-ru-ut 
#tr.ts: ammīnim ina bārût 
#tr.en: Why in the divination 
12. s,a-ba-at _iri#{ki}_ la et-me2-e-ti# 
#tr.ts: ṣabāt ālim lā etmêti 
#tr.en: of the siezing of the city are you not occupied? 
@reverse 
1. u3 ki-a-am u2-ul ta-asz-pu-ri-im# 
#tr.ts: ū kiam ul tašpurīm 
#tr.en: Further, in the following way you did not write me,
2. um-ma at-ti-ma 
#tr.ts: umma attima 
#tr.en: thus you: 
3. _iri{ki}_ szu-u2 is,-s,a-ab-ba-at 
#tr.ts: ālum šu iṣṣabbat 
#tr.en: “That city will be siezed,” 
4. u2-lu-ma u2-ul is,-s,a-ab-ba-at 
#tr.ts: ūlūma ul iṣṣabbat 
#tr.en: or rather, “will not be siezed.” 
5. asz-szum ar-hi-isz# ka-sza-di-ia 
#tr.ts: aššum arḫiš kašādiya 
#tr.en: As to my quick arrival, 
6. sza ta-asz-pu-ri#-im 
#tr.ts: ša tašpurīm 
#tr.en: about which you wrote me, 
7. ar-hi-isz a-na _siskur2-re_ isz8-tar2 
#tr.ts: arḫiš ana nīqi ištar 
#tr.en: quickly for the sacrifice of Ištar 
8. a-ka-asz-sza-dam 
#tr.ts: akaššadam 
#tr.en: I will arrive.
